# Implementation Plan — Lead Growth V3.0 Enterprise CRM Transformation

This implementation plan details the transformation of Lead Growth into a full-fledged enterprise CRM and multi-tenant workforce platform matching HubSpot, Salesforce, and Zoho CRM standards across 16 core modules.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **V3.0 Enterprise Architecture Enhancements**:
> 1. **Enterprise Invitation System**: `WorkspaceInvite` entity and repository for tokenized secure invitation links (`/invite/accept?token=...`), expiration management, and registration setup.
> 2. **HubSpot-Style Lead Timeline Engine**: Chronological timeline of all events per lead (Created, Status Changed, Note Added, Call Made, Follow-up Scheduled, Converted) stored in `lead_activities` table.
> 3. **AI Lead Scoring Engine**: Automated scoring algorithm computing 0-100 scores and tier classifications (`HOT` 🔥, `WARM` ☀️, `COLD` ❄️) based on source, interactions, and follow-ups.
> 4. **Subscription & Billing Dashboard**: Workspace SaaS Plans (`FREE`, `PROFESSIONAL`, `ENTERPRISE`), usage tracking (Users, Leads, Campaigns), feature gating, and billing page.
> 5. **Security Center**: Admin Security Dashboard displaying active user sessions, login audit history, and failed login attempt detection.
> 6. **Interactive Task Kanban & Lead Timeline UI**: Enhanced visual cards and timeline components.

---

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend Layer (`/backend`)

#### [NEW] [WorkspaceInvite.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/entity/WorkspaceInvite.java) & [WorkspaceInviteRepository.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/repository/WorkspaceInviteRepository.java)
- Entity for managing tokenized workspace invitations (`id`, `workspace`, `email`, `role`, `token`, `status`, `expiresAt`, `createdAt`).

#### [NEW] [LeadActivity.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/entity/LeadActivity.java) & [LeadActivityRepository.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/repository/LeadActivityRepository.java)
- Entity for storing lead activity timeline items (`id`, `lead`, `actor`, `activityType`, `title`, `description`, `createdAt`).

#### [NEW] [LeadTimelineService.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/service/LeadTimelineService.java) & [LeadTimelineController.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/controller/LeadTimelineController.java)
- Service and controller for logging lead timeline events and fetching chronological activity history per lead.

#### [NEW] [LeadScoringService.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/service/LeadScoringService.java)
- Service to compute AI Lead Quality scores (0-100), quality tiers (`HOT`, `WARM`, `COLD`), and conversion probabilities based on source platform, interaction history, and follow-ups.

#### [NEW] [BillingService.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/service/BillingService.java) & [BillingController.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/controller/BillingController.java)
- Subscription plan management (`FREE`, `PROFESSIONAL`, `ENTERPRISE`), usage quota calculations, and billing plan upgrade/downgrade endpoints.

#### [NEW] [SecurityCenterService.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/service/SecurityCenterService.java) & [SecurityCenterController.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/controller/SecurityCenterController.java)
- Admin Security Center endpoint providing active sessions count, failed login attempt alerts, and security logs.

#### [NEW] [InviteService.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/service/InviteService.java) & [InviteController.java](file:///e:/WEB/LeadGrowth/backend/src/main/java/com/leadgrowth/controller/InviteController.java)
- Endpoints for creating invites (`POST /api/invites`), validating tokens (`GET /api/invites/validate`), and accepting invites (`POST /api/invites/accept`).

